1
00:00:08,844 --> 00:00:10,915
A friend phones with bad news.

2
00:00:10,995 --> 00:00:13,986
Before any thought, something
in me turns toward them.

3
00:00:14,066 --> 00:00:17,659
Then comes the harder part:
knowing what would actually help.

4
00:00:18,472 --> 00:00:21,100
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

5
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:25,058
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

6
00:00:25,868 --> 00:00:30,507
Six sections have looked at dependent
arising as a view. What is formed.

7
00:00:30,587 --> 00:00:33,591
What a phenomenon is. Mind and matter.

8
00:00:33,671 --> 00:00:35,480
The logic of dependency.

9
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:38,469
And the twelve links, as
the tradition teaches them,

10
00:00:38,549 --> 00:00:40,579
and as Nāgārjuna reads them.

11
00:00:41,376 --> 00:00:44,004
Almost nothing has been
said about compassion.

12
00:00:44,084 --> 00:00:46,531
That is a gap, and a serious one.

13
00:00:46,611 --> 00:00:49,942
Nāgārjuna's own Middle Way
ends with a bow to the Buddha,

14
00:00:50,022 --> 00:00:52,482
who out of compassion
taught the true Dharma,

15
00:00:52,562 --> 00:00:54,797
so that all views could be let go.

16
00:00:55,612 --> 00:00:59,789
So this last section turns to two
things a view like this must face.

17
00:00:59,869 --> 00:01:02,262
Here, in Part 1, compassion.

18
00:01:02,342 --> 00:01:06,084
In Part 2, the strongest
objections, fairly answered.

19
00:01:06,896 --> 00:01:08,981
First, what I will not say.

20
00:01:09,061 --> 00:01:12,024
I will not say that
emptiness causes compassion.

21
00:01:12,104 --> 00:01:14,239
Emptiness does not cause anything.

22
00:01:14,319 --> 00:01:16,698
It is not a power behind things.

23
00:01:16,778 --> 00:01:20,031
And seeing it is not a switch
that turns kindness on.

24
00:01:20,844 --> 00:01:23,404
But emptiness takes
nothing from compassion.

25
00:01:23,484 --> 00:01:28,214
When someone we love speaks kindly, we
imagine a fixed self behind the words,

26
00:01:28,294 --> 00:01:33,010
who really means them. The kindness
is felt, and no such ground is found.

27
00:01:33,090 --> 00:01:34,509
Nothing is missing.

28
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:37,812
And emptiness removes the excuses.

29
00:01:37,892 --> 00:01:39,416
It isn't really happening.

30
00:01:39,496 --> 00:01:42,676
They are only appearances.
There is no one there.

31
00:01:42,756 --> 00:01:46,186
Each of these needs a world where
what is empty does not count.

32
00:01:46,988 --> 00:01:51,804
In the world this series has described,
what is empty is exactly what counts.

33
00:01:51,884 --> 00:01:55,920
What appears, vividly, working,
with nothing behind it.

34
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,698
A car injures, and the grief of
the family is not an illusion.

35
00:01:59,778 --> 00:02:03,819
Nothing waits outside the chain of
conditions to absorb what we do.

36
00:02:04,632 --> 00:02:07,355
As I see it, compassion is conventional.

37
00:02:07,435 --> 00:02:11,649
And conventional does not mean
merely agreed, or less than real.

38
00:02:11,729 --> 00:02:16,214
For the logic of dependency, conventional
truth is the only kind of validity there

39
00:02:16,294 --> 00:02:18,501
is, and it is fully valid.

40
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:22,472
The suffering of a being
is conventional, and real.

41
00:02:22,552 --> 00:02:25,746
The help that relieves it
is conventional, and real.

42
00:02:25,826 --> 00:02:28,504
Compassion meets suffering
where suffering is:

43
00:02:28,584 --> 00:02:32,449
among bodies, words, situations and needs.

44
00:02:33,248 --> 00:02:36,211
So compassion is not a
quality of the ultimate,

45
00:02:36,291 --> 00:02:39,477
sitting behind appearances,
waiting to be uncovered.

46
00:02:39,557 --> 00:02:43,512
And it is not a substance in the
heart that runs low, or fills up.

47
00:02:43,592 --> 00:02:46,053
It is a responsiveness
to the conventional.

48
00:02:46,133 --> 00:02:49,246
To this person, this pain, this situation,

49
00:02:49,326 --> 00:02:50,976
as it actually is for them.

50
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:55,305
That is also why no being's
suffering can be brushed aside.

51
00:02:55,385 --> 00:02:57,588
No single world is the given one.

52
00:02:57,668 --> 00:03:01,079
The hungry ghost's suffering
is real for the hungry ghost.

53
00:03:01,159 --> 00:03:03,824
It cannot be dismissed
as not really happening,

54
00:03:03,904 --> 00:03:05,567
because it is not ours.

55
00:03:06,376 --> 00:03:09,190
The first half of compassion, as I see it,

56
00:03:09,270 --> 00:03:10,906
is openness of the heart.

57
00:03:11,708 --> 00:03:15,871
This is not a feeling made on purpose,
and not an attitude to keep up.

58
00:03:15,951 --> 00:03:18,806
Openness is not a virtue added on top.

59
00:03:18,886 --> 00:03:21,429
It is what being dependent already means.

60
00:03:21,509 --> 00:03:24,295
When the habit of standing
apart is not imposed,

61
00:03:24,375 --> 00:03:26,256
the heart is already open.

62
00:03:27,072 --> 00:03:31,584
In Section 3, the gap between mind
and matter turned out to be made by a

63
00:03:31,664 --> 00:03:35,402
framework, one that defines
them as inherently different,

64
00:03:35,482 --> 00:03:37,200
each existing by itself.

65
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:39,741
The interaction itself is seamless.

66
00:03:39,821 --> 00:03:43,224
No one has ever had to work at
joining their mind to their body.

67
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:47,260
The gap between self and
other is made the same way.

68
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:52,328
Defined as two selves, each complete
on its own side, they need a bridge.

69
00:03:52,408 --> 00:03:55,253
And compassion becomes the
effort of building one.

70
00:03:56,048 --> 00:03:59,569
Seen as they arise, the
friend's voice, the bad news,

71
00:03:59,649 --> 00:04:01,991
and the turning toward
them are one movement.

72
00:04:02,071 --> 00:04:03,690
Nothing has to cross.

73
00:04:03,770 --> 00:04:08,409
Dōgen calls this identity action:
not separating oneself from others.

74
00:04:09,204 --> 00:04:12,444
And this openness shows
itself as the habit loosens.

75
00:04:12,524 --> 00:04:14,522
It is not produced by insight.

76
00:04:14,602 --> 00:04:16,551
But it is no longer blocked.

77
00:04:17,344 --> 00:04:19,103
The other half is learning.

78
00:04:19,916 --> 00:04:23,590
An open heart does not, by
itself, know what to do.

79
00:04:23,670 --> 00:04:26,838
A friend in grief may
need words, or silence,

80
00:04:26,918 --> 00:04:29,704
or a meal, or to be left alone for a day.

81
00:04:29,784 --> 00:04:32,802
A child may need comfort, or a firm no.

82
00:04:32,882 --> 00:04:36,743
A stranger's customs may make
my kindness land as an insult.

83
00:04:36,823 --> 00:04:41,122
Good will that does not know the
situation can miss, and sometimes harm.

84
00:04:41,928 --> 00:04:45,901
So compassion learns the conventional
as it meets each situation.

85
00:04:45,981 --> 00:04:48,986
What this person needs.
How things work here.

86
00:04:49,066 --> 00:04:52,006
What helps, and what
only feels like helping.

87
00:04:52,804 --> 00:04:57,266
This learning never ends, because
situations never repeat exactly.

88
00:04:57,346 --> 00:05:00,514
It is the same skill the
whole series has pointed at:

89
00:05:00,594 --> 00:05:03,747
seeing conditions clearly,
and arranging them well.

90
00:05:03,827 --> 00:05:07,040
Compassion is that path,
turned toward others.

91
00:05:07,856 --> 00:05:10,620
And because it is learned,
it can be cultivated.

92
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:14,193
It deepens with practice,
with mistakes, with attention.

93
00:05:14,273 --> 00:05:19,510
So, does compassion simply show
itself, or is it trained? Both.

94
00:05:20,316 --> 00:05:23,705
Three traditions I respect have
said this in their own ways.

95
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:29,023
Tsongkhapa teaches compassion as
something trained, step by step.

96
00:05:29,103 --> 00:05:31,768
Seeing every being as
having been one's mother.

97
00:05:31,848 --> 00:05:34,947
Remembering their kindness.
Wishing to repay it.

98
00:05:35,027 --> 00:05:39,499
Love, compassion, a special
resolve, and the awakened mind.

99
00:05:39,579 --> 00:05:41,129
Compassion is method.

100
00:05:41,209 --> 00:05:43,303
The view of emptiness is wisdom.

101
00:05:43,383 --> 00:05:45,862
Both are needed, like two wings.

102
00:05:46,676 --> 00:05:51,936
Mipham, with Dzogchen in view, describes
the nature of mind as empty in essence,

103
00:05:52,016 --> 00:05:56,138
cognizant by nature, and unobstructed
in its compassionate energy.

104
00:05:56,218 --> 00:05:59,277
Compassion is one aspect
of the nature itself.

105
00:05:59,357 --> 00:06:02,787
Realization reveals it,
rather than producing it.

106
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:08,837
Dōgen speaks of compassion mostly
as conduct. Giving. Kind speech.

107
00:06:08,917 --> 00:06:12,709
Beneficial action. And not
separating oneself from others.

108
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:16,568
To the monastery cook he asks
for three minds in every task:

109
00:06:16,648 --> 00:06:20,399
the joyful mind, the nurturing
mind, and the great mind.

110
00:06:20,479 --> 00:06:23,321
For him, practice and awakening are one.

111
00:06:23,401 --> 00:06:27,157
Compassion is how awakening
acts, in each ordinary deed.

112
00:06:27,964 --> 00:06:32,399
Where do I stand? With Tsongkhapa,
that compassion is trained,

113
00:06:32,479 --> 00:06:35,674
and that care should never be
assumed to come automatically.

114
00:06:35,754 --> 00:06:39,166
With Mipham, that it is
unobstructed responsiveness,

115
00:06:39,246 --> 00:06:41,407
though I read his words without a ground:

116
00:06:41,487 --> 00:06:45,551
not a quality sitting in a basis,
but the openness of what appears.

117
00:06:45,631 --> 00:06:48,595
With Dōgen, that it
lives in ordinary acts.

118
00:06:48,675 --> 00:06:52,376
And with all three, that
it is empty, and works.

119
00:06:53,192 --> 00:06:56,649
So compassion is not a
source, sending kindness out.

120
00:06:56,729 --> 00:07:00,997
It is one of the conditions that meet, as
the friend's voice and the bad news are

121
00:07:01,077 --> 00:07:01,839
others.

122
00:07:01,919 --> 00:07:05,820
When they meet with an open heart that has
learned something of how the world works,

123
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:07,100
help appears.

124
00:07:07,812 --> 00:07:10,549
Nothing stands behind it, producing it.

125
00:07:10,629 --> 00:07:13,742
And it is exactly as
valid, and as reliable,

126
00:07:13,822 --> 00:07:16,083
as the ringing of a
bell when it is struck.

127
00:07:16,888 --> 00:07:21,622
In practice. When someone's pain
reaches you, notice the first turning,

128
00:07:21,702 --> 00:07:24,421
before any thought. It needs no effort.

129
00:07:24,501 --> 00:07:26,989
When it is blocked, see what blocks it.

130
00:07:27,069 --> 00:07:30,499
Usually a self standing
apart, defending something.

131
00:07:31,316 --> 00:07:33,265
Then ask what would actually help.

132
00:07:33,345 --> 00:07:35,303
Not what would make me feel helpful.

133
00:07:35,383 --> 00:07:38,405
If you do not know, ask, or wait.

134
00:07:39,216 --> 00:07:42,062
Watch the excuses. It is their karma.

135
00:07:42,142 --> 00:07:43,787
It is all empty anyway.

136
00:07:43,867 --> 00:07:45,526
It is not my business.

137
00:07:45,606 --> 00:07:48,656
Notice how each one needs
something to stand behind it.

138
00:07:49,468 --> 00:07:52,123
And do not hold compassion
as a thing to own.

139
00:07:52,203 --> 00:07:55,185
It is a responsiveness,
and it is empty too.

140
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:00,000
This is Section 7, Part 1 of
the Dependent Arising series.

141
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:05,426
Next, in Part 2, the strongest objections
to this series, fairly answered.

142
00:08:06,228 --> 00:08:09,712
The teaching itself arose
this way. In dependence.

143
00:08:09,792 --> 00:08:12,230
On compassion, for those who suffer.

